==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Tetsukachi''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Adamankachi''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Tekachi is not great in its first form. While spammable and cheap, its only real use is Dodge, and even then its chance is rather low, at only  10%. If you're a fan of constant gambling, Tekachi can be usable, especially since it targets three common traits in [[Into the Future]], meaning it can still provide use in situations where other Pixies or [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] in general may fail. [[Surge Attack|Surge]] immunity doesn't help it much either, as if you're at the point where you need anything to deal with [[:Category:Surge Attack Enemies|Surge enemies]], you would most likely be better off using a more applicable meatshield like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]] or [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]].

==='''Evolved Form'''===
While evolving into Tetsukachi does make some improvements, namely an overall health boost and adding the Resistant ability, it still underperforms as a tanker. It has similar health to [[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolo]], but doesn't deal as much damage, meaning it can only be used for taking hits, whereas Gravolo can be used for damage and tanking. While 750k effective health at level 50 is on par with other Evolved Pixie tankers, Tetsukachi's Dodge ability only has a 10% chance to activate. Compared to Talented [[Aer (Uber Rare Cat)|Aervanta]], who has a 30% chance to Dodge, Tetsukachi's Dodge will rarely activate, leaving it unable to provide a notable enough boost to bring Tetsukachi up to par with the other tanker Pixies. Despite all this, Tetsukachi does have a few niche uses, such against [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]], [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] or [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] Surge enemies like [[St. Dober]], [[Pterowl Hazuku]] and [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]]/[[Techn-Old Hyena]] under specific circumstances, as it allows Tetsukachi to utilize all of its abilities as well as possible. Its low cooldown and cost also make it a bit cheaper than Gravolodon and more spammable than both Gravolodon and [[Yamii (Uber Rare Cat)|Yaminora]].

Overall, Tetsukachi isn't great, but it's usable, and it can shine if the situations are right. Its triple trait targeting gives it lots of usability, especially in [[Into the Future]] as mentioned before, and Surge immunity gives it some more usage later in the game.

==='''True Form'''===
Adamankachi provides very small buffs that, while slightly beneficial, do not fix the issues of the unit as a whole. Adamankachi's HP is only 10% higher than its Evolved Form, which is nowhere near enough to make it viable. While the Dodge chance increase from 10% to 20% is decent, it is still rather low and isn't enough to save this unit from mediocrity, especially with its low health. Lastly, its speed increase is practically meaningless and will rarely (if ever) find value.

Overall, Adamankachi is an underwhelming True Form and still a lackluster tanker.

